groups-members-add#errors","content":"Errors"},"198":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add-4","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add","content":"Put a person who is in your organization in a group you made, or in a group from your identity provider. They have what the group gives, and what the groups it is in give, straight away. Someone who is in through your identity provider or a group nested in this one gets a membership of their own too, which stays if the other one ends. Putting in someone who was already put in here changes nothing. Built-in role groups take people through their role, and Everyone and groups from a queue can't be changed here. If the group gives CLI Access, directly or through a group it is in, the response says that your organization limits command line use to people who have it, for good. For administrators."},"199":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add-5","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add#parameters","content":"| Name    | In   | Type   | Required | Description                              |\n| ------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `group` | path | string | yes      | The group's id, from the list of groups. |","table":"table-0"},"200":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-members-add#parameters","content":"| Name     | In   | Type   | Required | Description                               |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `person` | path | string | yes      | The person's id, from the list of people. |","table":"table-0"},"201":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-groups-me