with a cursor. Send the same search with every cursor. Someone with no role is listed with an empty list of roles. To find who can do something, give the permission as `has_access`."},"456":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list-5","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list#parameters","content":"| Name         | In    | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------ | ----- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `has_access` | query | string |          | Only people who can do this, given to them directly or through a role or group. A permission's id from the list of permissions, or its exact title. The id is the stable handle and titles can change, so scripts should use the id. Access limited to part of your organization, such as one queue, does not count. |","table":"table-0"},"457":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-list#parameters","content":"| Name     | In    | Type   | Required | Description                                         |\n| -------- | ----- | ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `search` | query | string |          | Only people whose name or email contains this text. |","table":"table-0"},"458":{"id":"/d