mand line use is limited to people who have it, and that taking it away later does not undo that. For administrators."},"486":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add-5","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add#parameters","content":"| Name     | In   | Type   | Required | Description                               |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `person` | path | string | yes      | The person's id, from the list of people. |","table":"table-0"},"487":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add#parameters","content":"| Name         | In   | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------ | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | path | string | yes      | A permission's id from the list of permissions, or its exact title. The id is the stable handle and titles can change, so scripts should use the id. |","table":"table-0"},"488":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add-7","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/access-people-permissions-add#response-200","content":"| Field  | Type            | Required | Description                                             |\n| ------ | --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | string, or null | yes      | Something to know about this change, when there is one