`service_levels` are slugs from the priority list. `service_levels` replaces both targets, so give both. A `null` resolution follows the organization's, but first response always needs a target. A queue cannot be archived or restored here. A rename is refused if another queue that is not archived has the name. Turning off automatic routing on the default queue is refused too. A rename can fail after part of it was applied; retry the same call to finish it. For administrators and queue leads."},"2140":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","content":"Omit a field to leave it as it is. Send `null` to clear `auto_assignment`, `awaiting_reply`, `marked_resolved`, `max_open_per_person`, `service_levels`. The two are different requests here, and only here. Everywhere else on this API an omitted field and a null field mean the same thing."},"2141":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-7","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#parameters","content":"| Name    | In   | Type   | Required | Description                              |\n| ------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `queue` | path | string | yes      | The queue's id, from the list of queues. |","table":"table-0"},"2142":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-8","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"What to change on a queue. Omit a field to leave it as it is."},"2143":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-9","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field             | Type                           | Required | Description                                                         