create-45","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create#response-201","content":"The ticket's service level clock: when a reply and a resolution are due."},"2496":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create-46","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create#response-201","content":"| Field          | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `breach_count` | integer | yes      | How many response windows ended late since the service level was last reset. A window that is late but still running counts once it ends. Compare `response_due_at` with the current time to find one. |","table":"table-7"},"2497":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create-47","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create#response-201","content":"| Field               | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolution_due_at` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | When the ticket is due to be resolved. Empty when no resolution target applies. |","table":"table-7"},"2498":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create-48","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create#response-201","content":"| Field               | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolution_paused` | boolean | yes      | True while the ticket is in a state that stops the resolution clock, such as on hold. When the clock starts again, `resolution_due_at` moves later by the working time it was paused. A change that restarts the clock and also moves the ticket to another queue or priority gives it a new due time instead. |","table":"table-7"},"2499":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create-49","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-create#response-201","content":"| Field             | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `response_due_at` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | When the response window that is running now is due. Empty when no response window is running. Some queues start a new window after each reply from the team. |","table":"table-7"},"2500":{"id":"/docs/api/202