--- | --------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `description` | string, or null |          | The full text of the request, in plain text. |","table":"table-1"},"2776":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-10","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field       | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `followers` | list of object |          | People who follow this ticket. A follower can read the ticket and hears about its changes. The requester and the assignee always follow it. People who have left the organization are not listed. |","table":"table-1"},"2777":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-11","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field  | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------ | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hold` | object, or null |          | Who has the ticket while it is on hold, when reminders to them start and after how much quiet. Empty unless the ticket is on hold. |","table":"table-1"},"2778":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-12","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                              |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | The ticket id people see in the product. |","table":"table-1"},"2779":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-13","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field      | Type            | Required | Description                     |\n| ---------- | --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `priority` | string, or null |          | Slug of this ticket's priority. |","table":"table-1"},"2780":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-14","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field   | Type                   | Required | Description                                  |\n| ------- | ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `queue` | string (uuid), or null |          | Identifier of the queue this ticket sits in. |","table":"table-1"},"2781":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-15","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field       | Type            | Required | Description            |\n| ----------- | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------- |\n| `requester` | object, or null |          | Who the ticket is for. |","table":"table-1"},"2782":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-16","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `routing` | one of `pending`, `settled` | yes      | Fixed values: `settled` once the ticket has a stored queue and a stored `state`, `pending` until then, while automatic routing may still change the queue, state or priority. A ticket just filed can show `state: open` while `routing` is still `pending`. |","table":"table-1"},"2783":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-17","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field           | Type   | Required | Description                                                             |\n| --------------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `service_level` | object | yes      | When a reply and a resolution are due, as the ticket's queue sets them. |","table":"table-1"},"2784":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-18","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field   | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `state` | string, or null |          | Slug of the state this ticket is in. A new ticket has none until routing opens it; the response that files it shows `open` ahead of that. Routing can still move it, and a ticket that routing could not open stays without one, so get the ticket again to see where it settled. |","table":"table-1"},"2785":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-19","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field         | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------- | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `synced_from` | string, or null |          | The other system this ticket is linked to. Known values: `freshservice`, `jira`, `servicenow`; `external` for a system not listed. |","table":"table-1"},"2786":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-20","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                      |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `title` | string | yes      | One-line summary of the request. |","table":"table-1"},"2787":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-21","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field        | Type               | Required | Description                   |\n| ------------ | ------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `updated_at` | string (date-time) | yes      | When the ticket last changed. |","table":"table-1"},"2788":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-22","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type            | Required | Description                                                                    |\n| --------- | --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `web_url` | string, or null |          | Link that opens this ticket in the web app. Null when the link can't be built. |","table":"table-1"},"2789":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-23","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"A person, as they appear in a response."},"2790":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-24","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field          | Type   | Required | Description                                     |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `display_name` | string | yes      | How this person's name is shown in the product. |","table":"table-2"},"2791":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-25","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | This person's stable id. Pass it as `assignee`, `delegate`, in `followers` or as a people path to refer to them. |","table":"table-2"},"2792":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-26","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"What this caller may do to this ticket, right now."},"2793":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-27","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field             | Type           | Required | Description                                   |\n| ----------------- | -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `editable_fields` | list of string | yes      | Fields this caller can change on this ticket. |","table":"table-3"},"2794":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-28","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field         | Type           | Required | Description                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `transitions` | list of string | yes      | States this caller can move this ticket to. |","table":"table-3"},"2795":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-29","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"A person, as they appear in a response."},"2796":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-30","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field          | Type   | Required | Description                                     |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `display_name` | string | yes      | How this person's name is shown in the product. |","table":"table-4"},"2797":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-31","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | This person's stable id. Pass it as `assignee`, `delegate`, in `followers` or as a people path to refer to them. |","table":"table-4"},"2798":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-32","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"Who has a ticket on hold, when reminders to them start, and after how much quiet."},"2799":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-33","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field      | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------- | --------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `delegate` | object, or null | yes      | The person the ticket was handed to while it is on hold. They are the one reminded. Empty when no one was named, or when the person has left the organization. |","table":"table-5"},"2800":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-34","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field            | Type             | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `reminder_hours` | integer, or null | yes      | How many hours the ticket can go without activity before the delegate is reminded. New activity starts the count again. Empty when this ticket has no setting of its own, which means the queue's setting applies. |","table":"table-5"},"2801":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-35","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field   | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------- | --------------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `until` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | Reminders to the delegate wait until this time. The ticket stays on hold after it, until someone moves it on. Empty when reminders are not delayed. |","table":"table-5"},"2802":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-36","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"A person, as they appear in a response."},"2803":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-37","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field          | Type   | Required | Description                                     |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `display_name` | string | yes      | How this person's name is shown in the product. |","table":"table-6"},"2804":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-38","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | This person's stable id. Pass it as `assignee`, `delegate`, in `followers` or as a people path to refer to them. |","table":"table-6"},"2805":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-39","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"The ticket's service level clock: when a reply and a resolution are due."},"2806":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-40","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field          | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `breach_count` | integer | yes      | How many response windows ended late since the service level was last reset. A window that is late but still running counts once it ends. Compare `response_due_at` with the current time to find one. |","table":"table-7"},"2807":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-41","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field               | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolution_due_at` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | When the ticket is due to be resolved. Empty when no resolution target applies. |","table":"table-7"},"2808":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-42","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field               | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolution_paused` | boolean | yes      | True while the ticket is in a state that stops the resolution clock, such as on hold. When the clock starts again, `resolution_due_at` moves later by the working time it was paused. A change that restarts the clock and also moves the ticket to another queue or priority gives it a new due time instead. |","table":"table-7"},"2809":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-43","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#response-200","content":"| Field             | Type                        | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `response_due_at` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | When the response window that is running now is due. Empty when no response window is running. Some queues start a new window after each reply from the team. |","table":"table-7"},"2810":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-44","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"A failed call answers with a problem body: a stable `code` to branch on, a `detail` for people, and `retryable`, which is advice for that one response."},"2811":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-45","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"| Code                   | HTTP status | Meaning                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE` | 409         | This action is not available on this record right now. The response says why. |","table":"table-8"},"2812":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-46","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"| Code              | HTTP status | Meaning                                                                                             |\n| ----------------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `FEATURE_RETIRED` | 410         | This feature has been removed and no longer answers. Use its replacement if the response names one. |","table":"table-8"},"2813":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-47","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"| Code                    | HTTP status | Meaning                                                                                                    |\n| ----------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `IDEMPOTENCY_IN_FLIGHT` | 409         | An earlier request with this idempotency key is still running. Wait, then send it again with the same key. |","table":"table-8"},"2814":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-48","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"| Code                       | HTTP status | Meaning                                                                       |\n| -------------------------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_MISMATCH` | 422         | This idempotency key was already used for a different request. Use a new key. |","table":"table-8"},"2815":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge-49","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-nudge#errors","content":"| Code                       | HTTP status | Meaning     