r. Send one of the dates in published_versions. |","table":"table-3"},"3531":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","type":"page","content":"List who has access to a workflow","breadcrumbs":["Docs","API reference","2026-09-14","Workflow access"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list"},"3532":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-0","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","content":"GET /workflows/{workflow}/grants"},"3533":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-1","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#parameters","content":"Parameters"},"3534":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-2","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"Response 200"},"3535":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-3","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#errors","content":"Errors"},"3536":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-4","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","content":"Who can see, run or change a workflow: the people and groups given access to this workflow, and the access that covers every workflow in your organization. A person is shown by id, because their name is not part of the answer. Access given by someone else, or through a role, is listed too, with who gave it. You need view, edit or publish access to the workflow. A workflow you cannot see, or one that does not exist, is reported as not found."},"3537":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-5","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#parameters","content":"| Name       | In   | Type   | Required | Description                                    |\n| ---------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `workflow` | path | string | yes      | The workflow's id, from the list of workflows. |","table":"table-0"},"3538":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field    | Type           | Required | Description                                                         |\n| -------- | -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grants` | list of object | yes      | Access given on this workflow alone. A grant can be one of several. |","table":"table-1"},"3539":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-7","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field       | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `inherited` | list of object | yes      | Access that covers every workflow in your organization and so reaches this one. It cannot be taken away from here. |","table":"table-1"},"3540":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-8","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"One thing a person or group can do with a workflow."},"3541":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-9","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field      | Type                                                                         | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `given_by` | list of one of `workflow_access`, `admin`, `availability`, `other` or string | yes      | Who put this access there, one name for each who did: `workflow_access` (the workflows product itself: the access settings in the web app or this API), `availability` (everyone's right to start a workflow that is offered to everyone), `admin` (an administrator, from the access settings of your organization) or `other`. Only access that is just `workflow_access` can be taken away here. Empty for access that covers every workflow, which is not listed by who gave it. |","table":"table-2"},"3542":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-10","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required | Description         |\n| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `grantee` | object | yes      | Who a grant is for. |","table":"table-2"},"3543":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-11","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field        | Type                                                                  | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | one of `view`, `run`, `edit`, `publish`, `self_service_run` or string | yes      | What they can do. `view` lets them see the workflow and its versions. `run` lets them start it. `edit` lets them change its draft. `publish` lets them publish versions, turn it on and off, delete it and change who has access. `self_service_run` lets them start it when it is offered to everyone. |","table":"table-2"},"3544":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-12","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"One thing a person or group can do with a workflow."},"3545":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-13","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field      | Type                                                                         | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `given_by` | list of one of `workflow_access`, `admin`, `availability`, `other` or string | yes      | Who put this access there, one name for each who did: `workflow_access` (the workflows product itself: the access settings in the web app or this API), `availability` (everyone's right to start a workflow that is offered to everyone), `admin` (an administrator, from the access settings of your organization) or `other`. Only access that is just `workflow_access` can be taken away here. Empty for access that covers every workflow, which is not listed by who gave it. |","table":"table-3"},"3546":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-14","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required | Description         |\n| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `grantee` | object | yes      | Who a grant is for. |","table":"table-3"},"3547":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-15","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list#response-200","content":"| Field        | Type                                                                  | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | one of `view`, `run`, `edit`, `publish`, `self_service_run` or string | yes      | What they can do. `view` lets them see the workflow and its versions. `run` lets them start it. `edit` lets them change its draft. `publish` lets them publish versions, turn it on and off, delete it and change who has access. `self_service_run` lets them start it when it is offered to everyone. |","table":"table-3"},"3548":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list-16","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-grants-list","tags":[],"t