-add-4","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add","content":"Give one person in your organization a permission for the whole organization, by the permission's id or exact title. They have it straight away. Giving someone what you already gave them changes nothing. Something they already have through a role, a group or Everyone, or that another system gave them, can't be added here. Giving Manage access lets them change who can do what. If the permission is CLI Access, the response says that once anyone in your organization has it, command line use is limited to people who have it, and that taking it away later does not undo that. For administrators."},"4476":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add-5","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add#parameters","content":"| Name     | In   | Type   | Required | Description                               |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `person` | path | string | yes      | The person's id, from the list of people. |","table":"table-0"},"4477":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add-6","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/access-people-permissions-add#parameters","content":"| Name         | In   | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------ | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permission` | path | string | yes      | A permission's id from the list of permissions, or its exact title. The id is the stab