--------------------------------- |\n| A token         | `stlabs login --with-token` | A script that already has a token. |"],[7908,"| To sign in with | Run                     | Use it for                                                                                 |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| A code          | `stlabs login --device` | A machine with no browser. Open the address it prints on another device and type the code. |"],[7907,"| To sign in with | Run            | Use it for         |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ------------------ |\n| A browser       | `stlabs login` | Your own computer. |"],[8053,"| Variable              | What it does                                                           |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_ORGANIZATION` | The organization to act on. It takes precedence over `stlabs org set`. |"],[8058,"| Variable            | What it does                                                                                          |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_HYPERLINKS` | `0` turns links off anywhere and `1` turns them on anywhere. By default, links follow the color rule. |"],[8056,"| Variable            | What it does                                                                                |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` | An absolute path that replaces `~/.claude` for the agent skill. A relative path is refused. |"],[8059,"| Variable            | What it does                                                                       |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_NO_NOTICES` | `1` hides every notice, including the warning about a command the API is retiring. |"],[8060,"| Variable           | What it does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_TELEMETRY` | `stlabs` sends crash reports, and looks once a day for a notice, without being asked. `0` stops both, so no update notice is shown either. `print` shows each crash report without sending it. `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` has the same effect as `0`. |"],[8062,"| Variable           | What it does                                      |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `VISUAL`, `EDITOR` | The editor that opens for a comment with no text. |"],[8055,"| Variable          | What it does                                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` | Where the `stlabs` settings folder goes when `STLABS_CONFIG` is not set. The default is `~/.config`. |"],[8054,"| Variable        | What it does                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_CONFIG` | The path of the settings file. The default is `config.json` in a `stlabs` folder under `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`. |"],[8052,"| Variable       | What it does                                   |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `STLABS_TOKEN` | The token to use instead of the saved session. |"],[8057,"| Variable   | What it does                                                                                                            |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `NO_COLOR` | Any value except an empty one turns color off. This applies to tables and to `stlabs setup`. `TERM=dumb` does the same. |"],[8061,"| Variable  | What it does                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `COLUMNS` | The width of tables, on a terminal and when piped. Without it, tables use the window's width, or 80 columns when piped. |"],[8075,"| You see                                                                                                   | Why                                                                                                                                                                           | What to do                                                                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `stlabs: the keychain is not available.` Then, for a command that calls the API, `stlabs: not signed in.` | `stlabs` cannot read the keychain, so it finds no session. On Linux, no Secret Service is running, which is usual on a server. On macOS, the keychain is locked. Exit code 1. | On Linux, see Sign in on a Linux server. On macOS, unlock the keychain. In both, `STLABS_TOKEN` works without one. |"],[8067,"| You see                                                                       | Why                                                                                                                                         | What to do                                                                                              |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A 403 `PERMISSION_DENIED` that says the slug is not one of your organizations | `stlabs org set` saves a slug without checking it, so a wrong one fails on the first call to the API. A display name is often not the slug. | Take the slug from the name after `/org/` in your STLabs web address, then run `stlabs org set <slug>`. |"],[8065,"| You see                                                                 | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                       | What to do                                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A 401 from the API that ends `Run stlabs login, or check STLABS_TOKEN.` | The token in `STLABS_TOKEN` or your session is not accepted. Exit code 4. When the output is piped, the line reads `stlabs: the API refused the token (expired or invalid).` followed by the same advice. | Run `stlabs login` to sign in again, or check `STLABS_TOKEN`. |"],[8068,"| You see                                                                 | Why                                      | What to do                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A 403 with the code `PERMISSION_DENIED`, which says you are not allowed | You may have the wrong organization set. | Run `stlabs org status`, then `stlabs org set <slug>` if it is wrong. `stlabs` leaves this hint out when the refusal is about one field or one ticket, such as changing a title, because another organization would not change it. |"],[8064,"| You see                                                              | Why                                                     | What to do          |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `stlabs: your sign-in has expired or was revoked. Run stlabs login.` | Your saved session expired or was revoked. Exit code 1. | Run `stlabs login`. |"],[8074,"| You see                                                           | Why                                                                | What to do                               |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `warning: 'stlabs tickets list' will stop working on 2027-03-14.` | The API is retiring that command. It keeps working until that day. | Install the latest `stlabs` before then. |"],[8073,"| You see                                                        | Why                                                         | What to do                   |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Exit code 11 and a line that says to install the latest stlabs | The API has retired the API version this `stlabs` asks for. | Install the latest `stlabs`. |"],[8072,"| You see                                                        | Why                              | What to do                                   |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Exit code 11 and a line that says the command has been removed | The API has retired the command. | Run `stlabs --help` to see what replaces it. |"],[8070,"| You see                                           | Why                                                                                                           | What to do                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A 403 with the code `ELIGIBILITY_REQUIRES_PERSON` | You are not signed in as a person in the organization you chose, often because the wrong organization is set. | Run `stlabs org status`, and sign in as yourself with `stlabs login`. |"],[8069,"| You see                                        | Why                                          | What to do                             |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| A 403 with the code `ORGANIZATION_NOT_ENABLED` | The API is not set up for your organization. | Email support@stlabs.com to set it up. |"],[8066,"| You see                       | Why                                                                                               | What to do                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `stlabs: no organization set` | No saved organization, and `STLABS_ORGANIZATION` is not set. `stlabs` sends nothing. Exit code 1. | Run `stlabs org set <slug>`. |"],[8071,"| You see                   | Why                         | What to do                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stlabs: unknown command` | The command does not exist. | Run `stlabs --help`. `stlabs` suggests the closest command when there is one, as in `Did you mean 'stlabs tickets list'?` |"],[8063,"| You see                 | Why                                                                                            | What to do                                 |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `stlabs: not signed in` | You have no saved session, and `STLABS_TOKEN` is not set. `stlabs` sends nothing. Exit code 1.